within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L04A_Immunosuppressants.L04AD03_Voclosporin;
model Voclosporin_Mayo2014_PD_cna
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Mayo_2014 :: CNa (calcineurin activity)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 1.15,      // [pmol/min/mg]
    Emax = -0.87,  // [pmol/min/mg]
    EC50 = 0.000123,  // [kg/m3; ng/mL × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng/mL per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1300, Interval = 2.6),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Voclosporin_Mayo2014_PD_cna</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Mayo PR et al., <i>Journal of clinical pharmacology 54(5):537–545</i> 2014 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcph.237\">doi:10.1002/jcph.237</a>) — calcineurin activity [pmol/min/mg] against voclosporin ng/mL — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       1.15 pmol/min/mg drug-free response (baseline) (baseline immunosuppression, Q324)
  Emax  =       0.87 pmol/min/mg maximal effect term (Maximum CNa Inhibition, Q323)
  EC50  =        123 ng/mL    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (effective concentration, Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng/mL of voclosporin per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 1.15   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (123 ng/mL)  response 0.715
  exposure -> infinity  response 0.28</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Mayo_2014: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Voclosporin_Mayo2014_PD_cna;
